   "temperature_mush_liquid_fraction": {
    "description": "Temperature of the mush from enthalpy and liquid fraction (temperature_mush_liquid_fraction, icepack_mushy_physics.F90:457-471): zTin = (zqin + (1-phi)*rhoi*Lfresh)/(phi*(cp_ocn*rhow - cp_ice*rhoi) + rhoi*cp_ice) (F90:468-469), the linear inverse of enthalpy_mush_liquid_fraction. Constants as in the D-class CESM-coupled run (nuopc-cap overrides, ice_comp_nuopc.F90:415-450; bugs.md #11; see file description).",
    "params": ["qin", "phi"],
    "body": {
     "op": "/",
     "args": [
      {
       "op": "+",
       "args": [
        "qin",
        {
         "op": "*",
         "args": [
          {
           "op": "-",
           "args": [
            1.0,
            "phi"
           ]
          },
          306002900.0
         ]
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "op": "+",
       "args": [
        {
         "op": "*",
         "args": [
          "phi",
          2158359.41
         ]
        },
        1941536.59
       ]
      }
     ]
    }
   },
   "ice_conductivity_mush": {
    "description": "Mush heat conductivity (heat_conductivity, icepack_mushy_physics.F90:476-494): km = phi*(kb - ki) + ki with the liquid fraction phi = icepack_mushy_liquid_fraction(zTin, zSin) (F90:490-492), ki = 2.3 W/m/K the fresh-ice conductivity and kb = 0.5375 W/m/K the brine conductivity (F90:62-63). This is the ktherm = 2 law used by the mushy thermodynamics; the ktherm = 1 MU71/bubbly laws remain the ice_conductivity_mu71/ice_conductivity_bubbly templates.",
    "params": ["T", "S"],
    "body": {
     "op": "+",
     "args": [
      {
       "op": "*",
       "args": [
        {
         "op": "apply_expression_template",
         "args": [],
         "name": "icepack_mushy_liquid_fraction",
         "bindings": {
          "T": "T",
          "S": "S"
         }
        },
        {
         "op": "-",
         "args": [
          {"op": "const", "args": [], "value": 0.5375, "units": "W/m/K"},
          {"op": "const", "args": [], "value": 2.3, "units": "W/m/K"}
         ]
        }
       ]
      },
      {"op": "const", "args": [], "value": 2.3, "units": "W/m/K"}
     ]
    }
   },
   "dEdd_snow_fraction": {
    "description": "Horizontal snow fraction of the dEdd shortwave scheme (shortwave_dEdd_set_snow, icepack_shortwave.F90:3448-3454): fs = 1 when the snow depth hs = vsno/aice >= hs_min, reduced to min(hs/hs0, 1) when hs0 > puny. hs_min = 1e-4 m (icepack_parameters.F90:123); hs0 is the namelist transition depth (default 0.03 m F90:345, overridden to 0.0 in the D-class run, which leaves fs in {0, 1}); puny = 1e-11 (F90:36).",
    "params": ["aice", "vsno", "hs0"],
    "body": {
     "op": "ifelse",
     "args": [
      {
       "op": ">=",
       "args": [
        {
         "op": "/",
         "args": [
          "vsno",
          "aice"
         ]
        },
        {"op": "const", "args": [], "value": 0.0001, "units": "m"}
       ]
      },
      {
       "op": "ifelse",
       "args": [
        {
         "op": ">",
         "args": [
          "hs0",
          {"op": "const", "args": [], "value": 1e-11, "units": "m"}
         ]
        },
        {
         "op": "min",
         "args": [
          {
           "op": "/",
           "args": [
            {
             "op": "/",
             "args": [
              "vsno",
              "aice"
             ]
            },
            "hs0"
           ]
          },
          1.0
         ]
        },
        1.0
       ]
      },
      0.0
     ]
    }
   },
   "dEdd_effective_pond": {
    "description": "Effective pond area of the dEdd shortwave scheme (shortwave_dEdd_set_eff, icepack_shortwave.F90:3495-3637) for the sea-level pond tracer (tr_pond_sealvl, apondn = apndn) under snwredist = 'none' (the bulk-redistribution branch F90:3554-3578 is not exercised in the D-class run): apeffn = fpn after (i) the meltwater-use reduction fpn = (1 - ffracn)*apondn (F90:3603), (ii) the pond-ice snow taper asnow = min(spn/hs1, 1) applied only when dhs > puny and spn >= puny (F90:3606-3609; hs1 = 0.03 F90:346 is always > puny), (iii) the snow-infiltration branch (F90:3611-3628): rp = rhofresh*hpndn/(rhofresh*hpndn + rhos*hs), which zeroes the pond for rp < p15, otherwise remaps the pond depth by the retained-meltwater fraction hmx = hs*(rhofresh - rhos)/rhofresh with tmp = 1 for hpndn >= hmx, and (iv) the thin-pond mask fpn = 0 for hpn < hpmin (F90:3630-3635). The dhs input is the persistent snow-depth-difference tracer of F90:3591 with the initialization F90:3586-3590: dhs = hs - fsnow*dt when the lid ipn = apondn*ipndn exists and dhs < puny and fsnow*dt > hs_min (F90:3586-3588), spn = hs - dhs (F90:3589), and dhs reset to 0 when ipn*spn < puny (F90:3590); the taper condition uses the possibly-reset dhs with the pre-reset spn, exactly as in the Fortran. Constants: rhofresh = 1000, rhos = 330 (icepack_parameters.F90:66, 61), p15 = 0.15 (F90:59), hpmin = 0.005 (F90:242), hs1 = 0.03 (F90:346), hs_min = 1e-4 (F90:123), puny = 1e-11 (F90:36).",
    "params": ["aicen", "vsnon", "apondn", "hpndn", "ipndn", "ffracn", "fsnow", "dt", "dhsn"],
    "body": {
     "op": "ifelse",
     "args": [
      {
       "op": "<",
       "args": [
        {
         "op": "ifelse",
         "args": [
          {
           "op": ">",
           "args": [
            "hpndn",
            {"op": "const", "args": [], "value": 1e-11, "units": "m"}
           ]
          },
          {
